WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.494
Metacognition also appears before the work begins.

00:00:02.494 --> 00:00:06.599
Planning means choosing an approach that fits the task instead of automatically

00:00:06.599 --> 00:00:08.652
using the same strategy every time.

00:00:08.652 --> 00:00:10.362
Different tasks require different methods.

00:00:10.362 --> 00:00:14.467
Learning a concept, debugging a failure, writing a recommendation, reviewing a design,

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:18.914
and preparing for a difficult conversation all place different demands on attention, evidence,

00:00:18.914 --> 00:00:19.598
and time.

00:00:19.598 --> 00:00:21.650
Good planning starts with the outcome.

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:25.071
What are you trying to learn, decide, produce, or improve?

00:00:25.071 --> 00:00:26.781
What do you already know?

00:00:26.781 --> 00:00:27.808
What is uncertain?

00:00:27.808 --> 00:00:29.176
What resources will help?

00:00:29.176 --> 00:00:31.912
How difficult is the task likely to be?

00:00:31.912 --> 00:00:33.623
Where should you place checkpoints?

00:00:33.623 --> 00:00:38.754
These questions help allocate attention and time before momentum carries you into the wrong approach.

00:00:38.754 --> 00:00:42.517
Strategy selection includes choosing when to use notes, examples, diagrams, checklists,

00:00:42.517 --> 00:00:45.595
experiments, retrieval practice, peer review, or a worked example.

00:00:45.595 --> 00:00:49.358
A diagram may be the right tool when relationships are confusing.

00:00:49.358 --> 00:00:53.463
A checklist may help when steps are repeatable and easy to skip.

00:00:53.463 --> 00:00:58.936
A small experiment may be better than another long debate when the issue can be tested.

00:00:58.936 --> 00:01:00.988
The practical risk is strategy autopilot.

00:01:00.988 --> 00:01:05.777
People often use the method that feels comfortable, not the method the task requires.

00:01:05.777 --> 00:01:08.856
A strong metacognitive habit is to pause and ask,

00:01:08.856 --> 00:01:10.908
what kind of problem is this?

00:01:10.908 --> 00:01:12.619
Then choose the strategy deliberately.

00:01:12.619 --> 00:01:16.723
That small moment of planning can save hours of effort that would

00:01:16.723 --> 00:01:19.460
otherwise be spent pushing a mismatched method harder.
